{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1561366118,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI0MDEwNzY1Nw=="},"target":"325c7b86277414c93e971eb19c4c4eaac08209f893b195b3c1b354ba0882af3d","message":"I am using this functionality more and more, but it is rather clunky. For example, it is not easy to stream large outputs (think decompressing a remote archive and storing the output locally without making tmp copies, etc.\n\nI see two paths forward:\n\n1. Expose internal pieces, such as SSH command generation, so that could be used with an outside \"runner\".\n2. Add a dedicated `.run()` that sits on top of `subprocess.run()` and takes the same args.\n\n   https://docs.python.org/3/library/subprocess.html#subprocess.run\n\nThe later is PY3.5+ only, so we likely don't want to base internal functionality on it, but it would be very helpful in order to have the entire range of possibilities available via a standard interface, plus the connection handling functionality that we provide.\n\nWhat do you think?","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1561371096,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI0MDE1MDg4MA=="},"target":"325c7b86277414c93e971eb19c4c4eaac08209f893b195b3c1b354ba0882af3d","message":"I am using this functionality more and more, but it is rather clunky. For example, it is not easy to stream large outputs (think decompressing a remote archive and storing the output locally without making tmp copies, etc.\n\nI see two paths forward:\n\n1. Expose internal pieces, such as SSH command generation, so that could be used with an outside \"runner\".\n2. Add a dedicated `.run()` that sits on top of `subprocess.run()` and takes the same args.\n\n   https://docs.python.org/3/library/subprocess.html#subprocess.run\n\nThe later is PY3.5+ only, so we likely don't want to base internal functionality on it, but it would be very helpful in order to have the entire range of possibilities available via a standard interface, plus the connection handling functionality that we provide.\n\nIt also offers a cross-platform DEVNULL object (in addition to PIPE), which is really handy (PY 3.3+).\n\nWhat do you think?","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1561366064,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI0MzM1MTM4NTI="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1561371171,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwNDk0ODQ4MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3487#issuecomment-504948480"},"message":"Approach 2. looks much cleaner to me.\nAnd ... well, I'll not mention the ticking clock. Not at all.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1562247878,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwODQ4NzgzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3487#issuecomment-508487833"},"message":"Abusing this issue to leave a trace of a sneaking suspicion that something in this code is extremely suboptimal. I am running git-annex special remote test suite on two very similar implementations, one performing direct filesystem operations, one doing the closest analog through SSH connections to `localhost`. The difference in timing is extreme (80+ times slower via SSH). CPU utilization is \u003c20%. Will have to dig into this...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1570266736,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzODYzMjQ5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3487#issuecomment-538632496"},"message":"Closing \"question\"-type issue with a response, and no further activity.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1570266736,"metadata":{"github-id